comments.body:
This is because MAVSDK currently identifies itself as [MISSION_PLANNER](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/develop/src/core/mavsdk_impl.cpp#L317-L318):

```cpp
uint8_t MavsdkImpl::get_own_system_id() const
{
    switch (_configuration.load()) {
        case Mavsdk::Configuration::GroundStation:
            return MAV_COMP_ID_MISSIONPLANNER;
```

I believe that one should be able to set the system id through the [configuration](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/develop/src/core/mavsdk_impl.cpp#L246-L249):

```cpp
void MavsdkImpl::set_configuration(Mavsdk::Configuration configuration)
```

[`Configuration`](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/develop/src/core/mavsdk.h#L137-L142) is currently an enum class:

```cpp
    enum class Configuration {
        Autopilot, /**< @brief SDK is used as an autopilot. */
        GroundStation, /**< @brief SDK is used as a ground station. */
        CompanionComputer /**< @brief SDK is used on a companion computer onboard the system (e.g.
                             drone). */
    };
```

But maybe it should contain the sysid, too.

@julianoes: Do you have an opinion on that?

